{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1783446062,"nonce":"6zULArhoKyKp2wuK8kLQPvyqIXU=","message":"Root cause found and fixed (branch faster-dop, 2026-07-07).\n\nWhat allowed \u003e11 GiB on the 12 GiB card:\n1. The WDDM hard allocator cap governed torch-only against physical total:\n   cap = total - 1 GiB = 10.99 GiB of *torch reserved*, but ~1.0-1.15 GiB of\n   the card is non-torch (CUDA context, VAE, desktop; grows to ~2.1 GiB as\n   Triton/compiled kernel code loads OUTSIDE the caching allocator). Torch\n   legally filled reserved to 10.97 -\u003e device_used 11.99, free 0.\n2. Reserved churn: streamed-FP8 transients + compile fragmentation push\n   reserved ~0.5-1.3 GiB above allocated within each step; the plan margin\n   (1.2) was smaller than churn + non-torch growth.\n3. skip_sampling_guard=True in the smoke meant no reactive relief; the\n   per-step trim only runs at step boundaries.\n\nFixes (toolkit/memory_management/manager.py + new vram_budget.py):\n- Device-aware allocator cap: fraction from (total - hard - non_torch)/total,\n  non_torch measured at cap time; re-measured per phase AND re-tightened per\n  step-trim as kernel-code growth erodes it (observed 9.85 -\u003e 8.87 GiB).\n- Sampling plan margin gets a reserved-churn pad (+0.5 GiB default,\n  AI_TOOLKIT_SAMPLING_RESERVED_CHURN_PAD_GIB) -\u003e one more streamed block up\n  front instead of a mid-denoise demote.\n- Mid-denoise OOM recovery is now incremental (2 largest blocks per OOM,\n  AI_TOOLKIT_SAMPLING_OOM_DEMOTE_BLOCKS) with a retry loop in pipeline.py;\n  full streamed transition only when nothing is left to demote.\n- Training pre-step guard now trips when EITHER the DXGI LOCAL or the\n  physical mem_get_info signal predicts pressure (was DXGI-only when\n  available).\n- Traceability: two-cliff arithmetic extracted to\n  toolkit/memory_management/vram_budget.py (DeviceSnapshot, WddmMargins,\n  pure predicates); post-move floor no longer rebinds wddm_margin_bytes;\n  guard/trim thresholds resolved once per phase; pin_alloc refusals now\n  print budget-vs-OS reason. Tests: tests/test_wddm_hard_cap.py.\n\nValidation (scripts/smoke_krea2_ingraph_cuda.py --ab-eager --fp8-sampling,\n.codex/krea2_ingraph_cuda_smoke_ab10.json):\n- sampling peak device_free=1.18 GiB (acceptance: \u003e= 1.0; was 0.00 in all 4\n  baseline runs), device_used 10.82/11.99, torch reserved 8.76 \u003c cap 8.87.\n- measured compiled pass 0.495 s/forward vs eager 1.09 (old swing was\n  0.79-1.68 riding the cliff); mixed_resident_ingraph_compile path, FP8\n  native_calls=1024 fallback=0. No OOM, no demote.\n\nNew issues discovered during validation (separate tickets):\n- Non-FP8 (dequant fallback) sampling: torchao fp32 dequant transients\n  (~0.86 GiB/linear) OOM-spiral under the honest cap; previously they\n  silently paged.\n- After deep demotes, ingraph pack pin_alloc fails with CUDA\n  'resource already mapped' (pin registration collision).\n- SDPA: unmasked GQA attention dispatches to MATH backend on this\n  Windows/torch 2.12 build (flash unavailable, efficient rejects\n  enable_gqa, MATH outranks CUDNN in default priority).","files":null}]}